From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PrismML-Eng <contact@prismml.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml : PQ2_0 / PTQ1_0 support in the Vulkan, HIP and remaining backends

Vulkan dequant shaders and supports_op wiring, the HIP decode path for
Q1_0/Q2_0/PQ2_0 on AMD, and the supports_op / type-table updates the other
backends need so they correctly refuse the new types instead of crashing.

Provenance
----------
Source:   https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp
Branch:   prism
Range:    5ea87ddad22541a37053c7ba92b02ec1923617c6..9a9394a895b96003ca842a6041cb28ac49a108f7
Base tag: b10615 (the fork's base is b10615 plus one unrelated webgpu commit,
          which is NOT included here - this diff is the fork's own work only)
Part 5 of 10, split by file group from the full 14,759-line fork diff.
llama.cpp is MIT licensed; the fork carries the same terms.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index e8a5009b3..2cd015be1 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -4193,7 +4193,8 @@ static bool ggml_backend_hexagon_device_supports_op(ggml_backend_dev_t dev, cons
             break;
 
         case GGML_OP_GATED_DELTA_NET:
-            supp = ggml_hexagon_supported_gated_delta_net(sess, op);
+            // rows-indexed state read (src[6]) not implemented here
+            supp = op->src[6] == NULL && ggml_get_op_params_i32(op, 1) == 0 && ggml_hexagon_supported_gated_delta_net(sess, op);
             break;
 
         case GGML_OP_CUMSUM:
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/ggml-opencl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/ggml-opencl.cpp
index 64f3325b2..9d6d59fa2 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/ggml-opencl.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/ggml-opencl.cpp
@@ -7714,6 +7714,10 @@ static bool ggml_opencl_supports_op(ggml_backend_dev_t dev, const struct ggml_te
         }
         case GGML_OP_GATED_DELTA_NET:
             {
+                // rows-indexed state read (src[6]) and raw gates (op_params[1]) not implemented here
+                if (op->src[6] != NULL || ggml_get_op_params_i32(op, 1) != 0) {
+                    return false;
+                }
                 // Match the Vulkan backend: only F32 -> F32, S_v in {16, 32, 64, 128}.
                 if (op->src[0]->type != GGML_TYPE_F32 || op->type != GGML_TYPE_F32) {
                     return false;
